{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>On its two sides.</b> Rashi explained: its two corners that are on its two sides. And superficially this would mean four rings, for two are needed for each side. And this is difficult, for this altar was only one cubit long and one cubit wide, and if so, how could two men pass through one cubit? For regarding the Ark they needed to explain that the rings were fixed along its width so that the carriers would stand along its length, because along its width they could not stand, as it was only a cubit and a half — and all the more so regarding the altar, which was only one cubit. Rather, one must say that here they carried it with only two men, one for each side, and he would stand between the two poles, and the two ends of the poles between his two shoulders."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:17.670340815Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}